Day 24 – PHP if-else, elseif & Loops
What I Learned :

On Day 24, I learned how PHP control structures make applications intelligent by controlling decision-making and repetition.

These concepts form the backbone of:

1.Authentication
2.Authorization
3.Input validation

 if-else & elseif (Decision Logic) :
* Example :
<?php
$role = "user";
if ($role === "admin") {
    echo "Full Access";
} elseif ($role === "user") {
    echo "Limited Access";
} else {
    echo "Access Denied";
}
?>

 Loops (Repeating Logic Safely) :
 for Loop Example :
<?php
for ($i = 1; $i <= 3; $i++) {
    echo "Login attempt " . $i . "<br>";
}
?>

Security Notes :
Poor logic leads to broken authentication
Always limit loop iterations
Avoid user-controlled infinite loops
Use strict comparisons (===)

 Key Takeaway :
if-else controls access.
Loops control repetition.
Secure logic protects applications.

Learning Philosophy :

Think like an attacker. Build like a defender.
